<speak>It will go in the study, but I work on it elsewhere. My wife drew a firm line at having dust spread across the bookshelves. It has become an enjoyable excuse to leave the desk. There is a particular satisfaction in stopping because the light has gone rather than because another message has arrived. I am not especially accomplished at it. I have had to undo some of my own work, and that has been rather good for me. At the office, people tend to spare me from seeing those untidy intermediate stages.</speak>